  "broader": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/ins/3505",
  "definition": "Exemption from Unitary Reserves for Certain n-Year Renewable Term Life Insurance Policies",
  "effectiveDate": "2017-07-25",
  "historyNote": "#7419, eff 7-1-01; ss by #9516, eff 7-25-09; ss by #12219, eff 7-25-17",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Ins 3505.07",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins3500.html",
  "prefLabel": "Ins 3505.07 Exemption from Unitary Reserves for Certain n-Year Renewable Term Life Insurance Policies",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 3505.07 Exemption from Unitary Reserves for Certain n-Year Renewable Term Life Insurance Policies.\n\n(a) Unitary basic reserves and unitary deficiency reserves need not be calculated for a policy if the following conditions are met:\n\n(1) The policy consists of a series of n-year periods, including the first period and all renewal periods, where n is the same for each period, except that for the final renewal period, n may be truncated or extended to reach the expiry age, provided that this final renewal period is less than 10 years and less than twice the size of the earlier n-year periods, and for each period, the premium rates on both the initial current premium scale and the guaranteed maximum premium scale are level;\n\n(2) The guaranteed gross premiums in all n-year periods are not less than the corresponding net premiums based upon the 1980 CSO Table with or without the ten-year select mortality factors; and\n\n(3) There are no cash surrender values in any policy year.\n\nSource. #7419, eff 7-1-01; ss by #9516, eff 7-25-09; ss by #12219, eff 7-25-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins3500.html"
}
